  "conclusions": [
    "All fixed native counterfactuals completed with exact prefixes and balanced full-horizon passenger accounting.",
    "Among8 positive-vs-zero comparisons with nonzero actual cost differences, masked min-Q sign agrees4 times and disagrees4 times;4 cost ties provide no direction evidence.",
    "Highest-masked-Q candidate selection gives2 lower-cost,2 higher-cost and8 equal-cost interventions; aggregate single-intervention delta+16508 passenger-seconds, mean+0.393497s per departed passenger per event.",
    "Current evidence does not support replacing deterministic extraction with finite-candidate Q maximization or changing gate on critic preferences alone."
  ],
  "next_step": {
    "kind": "Training-target versus evaluation-objective consistency diagnosis before more extraction or training changes",
    "scope": "Trace current native reward labels, transition clocks, discounts and target backup against full-horizon2*wait+ride accounting; identify whether observed Q/order differences concern a different objective/continuation or a genuine estimation failure.",
    "training_updates": 0,
    "status": "Not started; fixed12-event experiment complete"
  },
  "limitations": [
    "All12 event cases share one previously-used diagnostic demand/SUMO scenario and are correlated; they are not12 independent generalization trials.",
    "Outcomes condition on adapted continuation and compare four fixed candidates. Means and sums of individual interventions are descriptive and cannot be added into a continuously deployed policy benefit.",
    "Critics estimate scaled undiscounted IQL/H2O+ continuation values, not calibrated cost labels under adapted deterministic continuation; sign disagreements with that continuation's outcomes do not alone prove Bellman inconsistency or implementation errors.",
    "Identical actions reuse outcomes; distinct actions with exactly equal actual costs are retained as cost ties. Q ties use the previously fixed candidate order for descriptive selection."
  ],
